      "current60_entire_literal": {
        "key": "verification.html::exercise-15",
        "source": "SafeLearning/verification.html",
        "ordinal": 15,
        "locator": "::exercise-15",
        "anchor": null,
        "line": 796,
        "label": "Exercise 15.1 — Derive the IBP affine rule and exhibit its joint looseness",
        "level": null,
        "source_sha256": "2b60f48b0b374ab75902df099a19d28289b1e107ba2e23187c2b1e348f7d52cb",
        "source_text": "\n      \n        Exercise 15.1 — Derive the IBP affine rule and exhibit its joint looseness\n      \n      \n        (a) Let $a\\in[\\underline a,\\overline a]$ and $z=Wa+b$. Derive the interval $[\\underline z,\\overline z]$ produced by IBP and show that each coordinate bound is attained. (b) For $W=\\begin{bmatrix}1&1\\\\1&-1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b=0$ and $a\\in[-1,1]^2$, describe the true image $\\{Wa\\}$ and find a point of the IBP box that is not in it.\n        \n          Show answer\n          \n            (a) Write $a=\\mu+\\delta$ with $\\mu=\\tfrac12(\\overline a+\\underline a)$, $|\\delta_j|\\le r_j=\\tfrac12(\\overline a_j-\\underline a_j)$. Then $z_i=W_{i,:}\\mu+b_i+W_{i,:}\\delta$ and $|W_{i,:}\\delta|\\le\\sum_j|W_{ij}||\\delta_j|\\le\\sum_j|W_{ij}|r_j=(|W|r)_i$ (triangle inequality, then $|\\delta_j|\\le r_j$). So $\\underline z=W\\mu+b-|W|r$, $\\overline z=W\\mu+b+|W|r$. Choosing $\\delta_j=r_j\\,\\mathrm{sign}(W_{ij})$ makes every term $|W_{ij}|r_j$ and this $\\delta$ is feasible, so $\\overline z_i$ is attained; $\\delta_j=-r_j\\,\\mathrm{sign}(W_{ij})$ attains $\\underline z_i$.\n            (b) $\\mu=0$, $r=(1,1)$, $|W|r=(2,2)$: IBP gives $z\\in[-2,2]^2$. The true image is the set of $(a_1+a_2,\\,a_1-a_2)$ with $|a_i|\\le1$, a square rotated by $45^\\circ$ with vertices $(\\pm2,0)$ and $(0,\\pm2)$ (equivalently $|z_1|+|z_2|\\le 2$). The IBP corner $(2,2)$ would need $a_1+a_2=2$ and $a_1-a_2=2$, i.e. $a_1=2$, which is infeasible. The box has area 16, the image has area 8: IBP doubles the area in a single layer, and the next layer may combine $z_1=2$ with $z_2=2$ as if both were reachable at once.\n          \n        \n      \n    ",
        "text_sha256": "af0c392619321c160b1fe74513832702f7fd24b1a07f44795e0625889f22bc71"
      },
      "discharged": true,
      "remaining_missing_clauses": [],
      "completion_correspondence": "Affine uses the exact source matrix[[1,1],[1,-1]], zero bias and common input square[-1,1]^2. It proves the actual image iff |z0|+|z1|<=2 in both directions using the explicit inverse; the four actual input corners have images(+-2,0),(0,+-2). The single box point(2,2) belongs to the actual IBP[-2,2]^2 and is not in that image. For the downstream affine row z0+z1, the actual attained greatest value on the joint image is2 while the IBP box has attained greatest value4. This explicitly associates the shared-input incompatibility with the exercise; it neither assumes joint independence nor asserts generic depth growth.",
      "old_claim_declarations_hypotheses_correspondence_or_status_changed": false
    }
